---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Limitcode Pro"
  description="Privacy policy for the Limitcode Pro Sublime Text plugin and limitcode.jawuil.dev website: zero code middleman, local API keys, license verification, and website analytics."
  canonicalPath="/privacy/"
>

  <Nav />

  <main class="privacy-page">
    <section class="container privacy-wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>Privacy &amp; Data Handling</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="last-updated">Last updated: November 12, 2026</p>

      <p class="privacy-intro">
        Limitcode Pro and the open-source Limitcode plugin are built by Jawuil at <a href="https://jawuil.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">jawuil.dev</a>.
        This policy separates
        <strong>what happens locally inside the Sublime Text plugin on your machine</strong> from
        <strong>what happens when you visit limitcode.jawuil.dev</strong>.
      </p>

      <h2>Summary (TL;DR)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero code middleman in the plugin:</strong> Your source code, file contents, prompts, and
          model responses go <strong>directly from your computer to your chosen AI provider</strong> (or stay
          100% on your machine when using local models like Ollama or LM Studio). Limitcode servers never
          receive, proxy, log, or store your code or prompts.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Your API keys &amp; OAuth tokens stay on your machine:</strong> Provider API keys and OAuth
          sessions (GitHub Copilot, OpenAI Codex, Google Antigravity) are stored locally in your Sublime Text
          configuration and are never transmitted to Limitcode servers.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Minimal license verification (Pro only):</strong> Limitcode Pro only contacts the Limitcode
          license server to verify your license key and enforce the 3-device activation limit, issuing a signed
          offline token valid for up to 30 days.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Zero editor telemetry:</strong> Neither the open-source edition nor Limitcode Pro collects
          usage telemetry, keystrokes, file names, or crash reports from inside Sublime Text.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h2>1. Data Handled by the Sublime Text Plugin</h2>

      <h3>1.1 Source Code, Prompts, and AI Provider Requests</h3>
      <p>
        Limitcode runs locally inside Sublime Text's plugin host. When you send a message or
        approve a tool call, the plugin makes direct HTTPS requests from your machine to the API endpoint of
        the provider you configured (such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, OpenRouter, DeepSeek, GitHub
        Copilot, or a local endpoint).
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not operate a proxy server for AI requests.</li>
        <li>We cannot see, read, or train on your code, prompts, diffs, or conversation history.</li>
        <li>Your conversation history and edit snapshots are saved locally on your computer inside your Sublime Text data directory.</li>
        <li>How your chosen AI provider processes your prompts is governed by that provider's own privacy policy and API terms.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>1.2 API Keys and Account Sign-In (OAuth)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          API keys entered in your Sublime Text settings and OAuth tokens obtained via account
          sign-in remain stored on your local filesystem.
        </li>
        <li>
          They are sent only to the respective provider endpoint to authenticate your requests and are never
          shared with Jawuil or third parties.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>1.3 License Activation (Limitcode Pro)</h3>
      <p>
        When you activate Limitcode Pro or when the plugin refreshes its periodic offline lease (every few days,
        with a 30-day offline grace window), the plugin sends an HTTPS request to the Limitcode license
        verification endpoint containing only:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your <strong>license key</strong>.</li>
        <li>A <strong>non-reversible cryptographic device fingerprint</strong> (derived from basic system identifiers) and platform label to count active seats (up to 3 devices per license).</li>
        <li>The plugin version number.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        No source code, project paths, environment variables, or editor contents are ever included in license
        verification requests.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <h2>2. Data Collected on the Website</h2>

      <h3>2.1 Website Analytics and Session Heatmaps</h3>
      <p>
        On <strong>limitcode.jawuil.dev</strong>, we use analytics tools to understand how pages are used and improve the site:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Self-hosted Umami analytics and own analytics scripts:</strong> Collects
          aggregated, privacy-friendly traffic metrics (page URL, HTTP referrer, browser/OS type, and country)
          without cross-site tracking profiles.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Microsoft Clarity:</strong> We partner with Microsoft Clarity to
          capture how visitors interact with the website through behavioral metrics, heatmaps, and anonymized
          session replays to improve site usability. Website usage data is captured using
          first- and third-party cookies and other tracking technologies. For more information about how
          Microsoft collects and uses this data, visit the
          <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <em>Note:</em> These web analytics scripts run <strong>only on limitcode.jawuil.dev</strong>
        and never inside the Sublime Text plugin.
      </p>

      <h3>2.2 Purchases, Billing, and Invoicing (Gumroad)</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>
          All orders are processed by <strong>Gumroad</strong> acting as our Merchant of Record.
        </li>
        <li>
          Your payment method details (credit card numbers, billing credentials) are handled directly by
          Gumroad and Stripe; we never have access to your full card number.
        </li>
        <li>
          When you purchase Limitcode Pro, Gumroad provides us with your name, purchase email address, country,
          order timestamp, and generated license key so we can deliver your license, verify activations, send
          critical release updates, and provide customer support.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h2>3. Open-Source Transparency</h2>
      <p>
        If you want to inspect how Limitcode interacts with Sublime Text views, settings, and provider APIs,
        you can audit the open-source pair-programming edition at any time on GitHub:
        <a href="https://github.com/Jawuilp/Limitcode" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/Jawuilp/Limitcode</a>.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <h2>4. Your Rights &amp; Contact</h2>
      <p>
        You can request information about your purchase/license records, ask to reset device activations, or
        request deletion of your support correspondence at any time by contacting:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:hola@jawuil.dev">hola@jawuil.dev</a></li>
        <li><strong>Author:</strong> Jawuil Pineda — <a href="https://jawuil.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener">jawuil.dev</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy-page {
    padding: clamp(32px, 6vw, 72px) 0 clamp(64px, 8vw, 120px);
  }

  .privacy-wrap {
    max-width: 860px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap .eyebrow {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--signal);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap .eyebrow .dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--signal);
  }

  .privacy-wrap h1 {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }

  .last-updated {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 2.2vw, 1.95rem);
    margin: 30px 0 14px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin: 22px 0 10px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap p,
  .privacy-wrap li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .privacy-intro {
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap p {
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .privacy-wrap ul {
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
    list-style: disc;
  }

  .privacy-wrap li {
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .privacy-wrap a {
    color: var(--signal);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.86em;
    background: var(--paper-deep);
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
  }

  .privacy-wrap hr {
    border: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
</style>
